hed": "2026-09-02T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMid0FVX3lxTE9iejFHZnZtQXZ4bW4wSDB1LTduVDNTUl9EbkhheWw2SXViYVdLNk43WFh1MmZnXzJBWlpIaHNOOTNkOVF0VzdPTF9ObkQzTjlIY0czQUV4RlcxY05NdkNFUVpiWVhtYUxKR2FZR0RNckY0cTdoNUpz?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 17.06, "prior_sd": 5.34, "poll_margin": 19.71, "poll_sd": 5.69, "poll_weight": 0.47, "fundamentals": {"margin": 18.65, "lean": 10.5, "environment": 4.15, "incumbency": 4.0, "money": 0.0}, "rating_margin": 16.0, "sigma_race": 5.5, "sigma_total": 5.91, "baseline_margin": 18.3, "analyst_adjustment": 0.2, "key_factors": ["Healey has led every 2026 poll by double digits, most recently 16-21 points", "All seven expert raters place the race in the Solid or Safe Democratic column", "D+14 state fundamentals plus a first-term incumbent seeking re-election", "Kalshi and Polymarket both price Healey's win odds around 96 percent"], "rationale": "Polling throughout 2026 shows Healey ahead by 16 to 29 points, with the latest surveys at 16-21, and every major rater calls the race Solid or Safe Democratic. Minogue's affordability and audit messaging has narrowed the gap only modestly, and the state's strong Democratic lean plus incumbency makes an upset highly unlikely.", "watch": "A late-breaking scandal, a standout debate performance by Minogue, or a sharp anti-incumbent shift could tighten the margin, though likely not enough to put the outcome in doubt.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Maura Healey (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Massachusetts Governor Maura Healey seeks a second term against Republican Mike Minogue, with independent Andrea James also on the ballot. The state's Democratic lean of roughly 14 points, combined with Healey's incumbency, frames the race as heavily tilted toward the incumbent. Every major race rater, including the Cook Political Report, Inside Elections, and Sabato's Crystal Ball, places it in the Solid or Safe Democratic column.\n\nPolling has been consistent all